# .dockerignore — keep these OUT of the image build context (task T7.1).
#
# This is a SECURITY and size control. Anything listed here is never copied
# into the image, even though the Dockerfile says `COPY backend/ ./`. Two of
# these lines matter enormously:
#   - backend/.env holds the real API key + bot token — it must NEVER be baked
#     into an image (images get pushed to registries). Secrets are injected at
#     RUN time via env vars instead.
#   - the local *.sqlite3 is your dev data — the container starts with its own
#     empty database on the mounted volume.

# Secrets — never in an image
**/.env

# Local dev database (the container uses a fresh volume-mounted DB)
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal

# Python virtual environment and caches (rebuilt from requirements.txt)
backend/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/logs/

# Node install + prior builds (rebuilt inside stage 1)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Git and tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/

# Docs and scripts aren't needed at runtime
*.md
dev-*.ps1
run-tests.ps1
